Why this fails at scale:

User Request	Query Tokens	Matched Tool	Problem
"send message to #general"	{send, message, general}	SLACK_ARCHIVE_A_PUBLIC_OR_PRIVATE_CHANNEL	"channel" matches, archive executed
"post to Slack"	{post, slack}	SLACK_SET_CHANNEL_TOPIC	"slack" matches, wrong action
"create GitHub issue"	{create, github, issue}	GITHUB_DELETE_AN_ISSUE	"issue" matches, destructive action
The token overlap approach has no understanding of intent (send vs. archive) or action semantics (create vs. delete).

